# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored — never commit real values.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build scope (V2). Which product this build is. Unset = 'mvp', the launch scope,
# so a plain `npm run build` produces the thing being shipped and the fuller build
# is the one you have to ask for. 'full' turns every north-star surface back on
# (Manage Media, Business Profile, location verify, reviews inbox, QR, notifications).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_SCOPE=full
#
# THE PREFIX IS THE SECURITY BOUNDARY:
#   VITE_*  is inlined into the JS bundle at build time → PUBLIC. Anyone who
#           opens the deployed site can read it. Only ever put public values here.
#   no VITE_ prefix → server-side only. Never reaches the browser.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini — SERVER SIDE. This is the one to set in production (Vercel → Project
# Settings → Environment Variables). It is read by api/gemini.js, the serverless
# proxy the app POSTs to; the key never leaves the server and never appears in a
# URL. Comma-separated if you have more than one key (they are tried in order).
# Unset → the app renders its written AI fallbacks, which is a fully working mode.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEYS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini — CLIENT SIDE. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. Setting this makes the browser
# call Google directly, which means THE KEY SHIPS IN THE BUNDLE. Convenient when
# running `npm run dev` without a serverless runtime; never set it in Vercel, and
# clear it before building anything you intend to deploy. The app logs a loud
# console warning whenever this path is taken.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEYS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (optional — without these the app runs on its built-in demo seed).
# Project Settings → API. The anon key is designed to be public; RLS is what
# enforces access, so run migrations 0002 + 0003 before pointing this at
# anything other than the demo seed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Product telemetry (optional — OFF unless this is set). The pilot's proof that
# Connect recovers business: the 8 events in packages/core/analytics.js, POSTed
# as batched JSON — { "events": [ … ] } — to whatever URL you put here.
#
# UNSET (the default) = ZERO analytics network calls. Nothing is queued, nothing
# is retried, nothing leaves the device; in `npm run dev` the events print to the
# console instead so you can watch the funnel while building.
#
# Public by construction (VITE_*, so it ships in the bundle) and safe to be: the
# module NEVER sends a phone number, a customer name, a review body, note text or
# a transcript — ids, enums and counts only, enforced in code. See the Telemetry
# section of README.md before pointing this anywhere.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_ANALYTICS_URL=

# ===========================================================================
# NATIVE (apps/mobile — Expo Go). Expo loads .env / .env.local from
# apps/mobile/, NOT from this directory, so these belong in a file there:
# apps/mobile/.env.local. Same flags and same defaults as the VITE_* pairs
# above; only the prefix differs, because that is the convention each bundler
# inlines. See apps/mobile/README.md §5.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* IS THE SAME SECURITY BOUNDARY AS VITE_*: inlined into the
# bundle, shipped to the device, readable by anyone holding the app. Nothing
# secret goes in any of them.
#
# Unset everything and the app runs on core's demo seed with written AI
# fallbacks — a fully working mode, and the one Expo Go demos use.
# ===========================================================================
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SCOPE=full
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=
#
# LOCAL DEV ONLY, and on native it is currently the ONLY way to get real AI:
# core's aiProxyUrl defaults to the relative '/api/gemini', which a native app
# has no origin to resolve, so the server proxy that holds the production key
# on web is unreachable from the phone. A key here calls Google directly from
# the device and ships in the bundle. Never set it in anything distributed.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEYS=
